course: dictionary
lesson: 15944
title: Unshod and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «unshod» is old-fashioned and formal, so you will mostly find it in stories and poems. You may not know it, but the context can help. The start un- often means not, as in unhappy. So unshod points towards something not being covered.
explain: «The unshod children ran along the beach, laughing as the waves splashed their feet.» The clues are ran along the beach and splashed their feet. Children splashing in the sea are usually not wearing shoes, so unshod must mean barefoot. Try the plain word in the sentence to check: «The barefoot children ran along the beach» still makes sense.
explain: The word can also be about animals. «The farmer said the horse was unshod, because it had no metal shoes on its hooves.» The clue is no metal shoes on its hooves. A horse with no horseshoes is unshod. Here the word is not about feet at all, but it still means not covered or fitted with shoes.
fact: Unshod means not wearing shoes; barefoot.
fact: An unshod horse has no horseshoes on its hooves.
fact: «Unshod» is formal and literary, so it is found mostly in stories and poems.
fact: The plain word for unshod, when it is about people, is barefoot.
fact: The start un- often means not, as in «unhappy», «unkind» and «untied».
exercise: «The unshod children ran along the beach.» What does unshod mean? | *Barefoot | Covered in sand | Wearing big wellies | Wet through from the sea
exercise: A farmer says «The horse is unshod.» What does that tell you? | *It has no horseshoes on its hooves | It can run very fast | It has painted hooves | It is wearing a saddle
exercise: «The unshod boy paddled in the stream.» Which plain word could replace unshod? | *Barefoot | Muddy | Sandy | Running
test: «The unshod boy paddled in the stream, his toes wriggling in the cold water.» What does unshod mean? | *Barefoot | Cold and shivering | Wearing wellies | Dripping with water
test: A horse with no horseshoes on its hooves can be called what? | Wild | Spotted | *Unshod | Shod
exam: Which sentence uses unshod correctly? | The unshod bus stopped at the corner | The unshod kettle boiled on the stove | *The unshod girl ran across the warm sand with bare feet | The unshod book was read in the library
